course: dictionary
lesson: 2425
title: Words about illness and the body
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to a special subject, like medicine. You may not know them, but the words around them give clues. «Many classmates live with long-term conditions, epilepsy, cystic fibrosis, ADHD, heart problems, and none of them is catching or anyone's fault.» The words long-term conditions and not catching tell you that cystic fibrosis is an illness that lasts a long time and is not passed on like a cold.
explain: Cystic is an adjective, a describing word. In «cystic fibrosis» it tells you which kind of fibrosis we mean. When you meet a new describing word, ask: what does it describe? Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «Cystic fibrosis is an inherited condition (passed down from parents) with thick sticky mucus (slime) in the lungs and gut.» The brackets explain two hard words for you. Writers often use brackets, dashes and commas to give meanings, so look for them.
explain: Read the whole sentence before you decide. «It is not catching, but two people with it keep apart so they do not pass lung germs to each other.» The word but shows a contrast: the illness itself is not caught, but the germs in the lungs can still spread. Clue words like but, so and because show how ideas connect.
fact: Cystic means to do with a cyst, a small sac or bubble in the body filled with fluid.
fact: In medicine, cystic can also mean to do with the bladder or the gall bladder.
fact: «Cystic fibrosis» is an illness people are born with, because it is inherited, passed down from parents.
fact: Cystic fibrosis makes thick, sticky mucus (slime) in the lungs and gut.
fact: People with cystic fibrosis take medicines and do physio to clear their lungs. It is not catching.
exercise: «Cystic fibrosis is an inherited condition.» What does inherited mean? | Very large | Cured by a doctor | Caught from a friend at school | *Passed down from parents
exercise: «It is not catching, but two people with it keep apart.» Why do two people with cystic fibrosis keep apart? | Because they do not like each other | Because it makes them very tall | *So they do not pass lung germs to each other | Because cystic fibrosis is catching like a cold
exercise: What is a cyst? | *A small sac or bubble in the body filled with fluid | A bone in the leg | A sticky sweet | A kind of medicine for the lungs
test: «Cystic fibrosis makes thick, sticky mucus (slime) in the lungs.» What is mucus? | Blood | Bone | Sweat | *Slime
test: Which of these is NOT true about cystic fibrosis? | *It is caught from a cough | People take medicines and do physio | It is inherited | It affects the lungs and gut
exam: Cystic is used in medicine to mean to do with a cyst, the bladder or the gall bladder. Which is the best meaning of cystic in «cystic fibrosis»? | A very cold type of weather | *An illness passed down from parents, with thick sticky mucus in the lungs and gut | A kind of loud music | A place where people go to swim
